==Norman==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|nrf}} {{m|fro|tirer||to draw, pull out with great effort, snatch violently, tear away}}, of uncertain origin; possibly from {{etyl|got|nrf}} {{m|got|*𐍄𐌹𐍂𐌰𐌽||to tear away, remove}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|nrf}} {{m|gem-pro|*teraną||to tear, tear apart}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|nrf}} {{m|ine-pro|*derə-||to tear, tear apart}}. If derived from the Germanic word, cognate with Gothic {{m|got|𐌳𐌹𐍃𐍄𐌰𐌹𐍂𐌰𐌽||to tear apart}}, {{m|got|𐌲𐌰𐍄𐌰𐌹𐍂𐌰𐌽||to tear down, remove}}, German {{m|de|zerren||to tug}}. Alternatively from a reduction of Old French {{m|fro|martirier}}, from {{etyl|LL.|nrf}} {{m|la|*martyrāre}}.

